{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/763370-litany-question","id":763370,"title":"Litany Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-11T12:57:16-08:00","id":763370,"title":"Litany Question","content":"So in a I'm in game the PC's were making plans to attack a pack of Spirals where they were wholed up. Recently a Bastet (PC) has become a tag along, and the alpha was explaining expectations he has for tag alongs (what he's ok with fera doing and what he's not ok). During this time, our Ragabash makes a comment about how the Alpha's expectations do not necessarily match his own actions (he's against the Fera putting themselves at risk in combat and it should go to the garou. However we have an npc on a redemption kick (Amenti) after sacrificing a Corax in a blood rite (basically performed the rite, was killed by the group and is back as &quot;Judged One&quot; now) is currently living with the alpha and is carrying his child. The Ragabash (Fenrir) cracked a comment about how this flies in the face of his &quot;fera safety&quot; policy. The Alpha (CoG) sees this as challenging the leader during a time of war, and wants to take it to a philodox....thoughts on the outcome?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 11-11-2015, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T13:01:43-08:00","id":763373,"title":"","content":"My first thought is that all of these characters are on crack and the Judges of Doom should come in and shank them all.<br /> <br /> My second thought is that the Ragabash criticizing their Alpha for breaking his own dumbass rule is right in their wheelhouse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T13:05:56-08:00","id":763380,"title":"","content":"So...why should the JoD kill off the Bastet and the Ragabash? I get the Ahroun.....<br /> <br /> In all seriousness I was more looking for input like the second comment and not so much generalized game bashing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 11-11-2015, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T13:53:00-08:00","id":763421,"title":"","content":"Ignoring the... odd set up there... the Ragabash is probably going to win this. As long as he doesn't push his role too far, he's acting within his Auspice's role; not violating the Litany. Declaring it a war where questioning is off the table is generally something done on the Sept level, not the pack level. The pack simply being planning an attack against the Wyrm's forces is standard Garou activity, and precisely when the Ragabash should be doing their job to make the plan as good as possible.<br /> <br /> If the Ahroun takes this to an external Philodox.... I'd imagine the Philodox is going to be a lot more concerned with the Litany issues of things like the CoG having a kid with a non-kin supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T14:06:02-08:00","id":763441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/763370-litany-question?p=763421#post763421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ignoring the... odd set up there... the Ragabash is probably going to win this. As long as he doesn't push his role too far, he's acting within his Auspice's role; not violating the Litany. Declaring it a war where questioning is off the table is generally something done on the Sept level, not the pack level. The pack simply being planning an attack against the Wyrm's forces is standard Garou activity, and precisely when the Ragabash should be doing their job to make the plan as good as possible.<br /> <br /> If the Ahroun takes this to an external Philodox.... I'd imagine the Philodox is going to be a lot more concerned with the Litany issues of things like the CoG having a kid with a non-kin supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Thanks, I was stuck in the philodox role and I wanted to see my options, granted I was thinking the Amenti is the real issue (it was something the CoG hasn't been advertising), and the comment being made outside of combat itself it wasn't a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T16:50:43-08:00","id":763586,"title":"","content":"Questioning is not disobeying. Ragabash or not, a character can get away with &quot;Hey, just sayin&quot; in a situation like this. At least that's how I would interpret it. Moreso the comment wasn't particularly a crack at the alpha's battle plans, rather at his peculiar life choices. As long as the Ragabash does what they are told I think they would be fine.<br /> Of course the major factors in such a ruling would be how much a hypothetical Philodox would like the alpha/the Ragabash/Fera. Since when was werewolf society about fairness and justice anyway?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29-vidyaraja","name":"Vidyaraja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T16:57:31-08:00","id":763589,"title":"","content":"To quote an old friend of mines' bonegnawer philodox &quot;if the litany breach don't fit, you must acquit&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T17:02:00-08:00","id":763590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vidyaraja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/763370-litany-question?p=763586#post763586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Questioning is not disobeying. Ragabash or not, a character can get away with &quot;Hey, just sayin&quot; in a situation like this. At least that's how I would interpret it. Moreso the comment wasn't particularly a crack at the alpha's battle plans, rather at his peculiar life choices. As long as the Ragabash does what they are told I think they would be fine.<br /> Of course the major factors in such a ruling would be how much a hypothetical Philodox would like the alpha/the Ragabash/Fera. Since when was werewolf society about fairness and justice anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> All good points also. I get the situation sounds off when abbreviated to the point it is for this forum. The Amenti was added to see what the group would think after they had already killed this individual as an enemy. The Ragabash was the only one to stick to &quot;this is not a good person, and what they did cannot be undone&quot;. The others decided that they liked the path of redemption idea and in some cases stopped hunting her, to well the Alpha's reaction to her, which no one (even the GM) saw coming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T18:02:20-08:00","id":763627,"title":"","content":"The Ragabash is quite entitled to be a snide bastard, especially when there is merit to his words. The trick is that he did not challenge the leader, even though he did make the leader uncomfortable. Challenge means &quot;if i tell you to do something i expect you to do it, no matter your reservations&quot; it's not &quot;Oh you can never ever say anything I don't like&quot;. Here the leader is trying to abuse the litany to his own benefit. The problem is... getting attention of a philodox will quite likely blow up in the leader's face.<br /> <br /> It's the Ragabash's job to make pointed comments and get people to think and react. I'm pretty sure the leaders choices could be quite easily construed as breaches of litany and endangering other Garou.<br /> <br /> I'm kinda curious what the exact setup here actually is, as it seems... complex :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T18:23:18-08:00","id":763640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/763370-litany-question?p=763627#post763627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ragabash is quite entitled to be a snide bastard, especially when there is merit to his words. The trick is that he did not challenge the leader, even though he did make the leader uncomfortable. Challenge means &quot;if i tell you to do something i expect you to do it, no matter your reservations&quot; it's not &quot;Oh you can never ever say anything I don't like&quot;. Here the leader is trying to abuse the litany to his own benefit. The problem is... getting attention of a philodox will quite likely blow up in the leader's face.<br /> <br /> It's the Ragabash's job to make pointed comments and get people to think and react. I'm pretty sure the leaders choices could be quite easily construed as breaches of litany and endangering other Garou.<br /> <br /> I'm kinda curious what the exact setup here actually is, as it seems... complex :P</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This game has been going on for a LONG time, I wouldn't mind answering questions though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T17:42:26-08:00","id":765250,"title":"","content":"&quot;Challenging the Leader&quot; means actually challenging for leadership of the pack/sept and removing the old leader in my opinion. Or some kind of great insubordination or mutiny so the leader can't lead. It doesn't mean someone can't disagree with a decision or argue against a plan while the pack is deliberating.<br /> <br /> Unless the sept has a very tyrannical view of leadership, Philodox is going to dismiss any complaint about the Ragabash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T08:59:46-08:00","id":766297,"title":"","content":"There's nothing for the Philodox to adjudicate: the Ragabash -- in typical trickster-sass fashion -- was pointing out a &quot;flaw&quot; in the Alpha's ongoing actions. (Mind you, I don't perceive his actions w/the Amenti -- unless I'm missing/misreading something -- as &quot;violating&quot;, so to speak, his general directives, but whatever...). The Ragabash was simply &quot;doing what he does&quot;. The Alpha needs to take a pill... which, perhaps phrased differently, is what the Philodox in question *should* tell him... (all-the-while slightly arcing an eyebrow at the pregnant Amenti -- sitting, say, somewhere in the back -- and then perhaps rolling his eyes *just a bit*... #ButWhatever #YoureTheAlpha )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T10:26:17-08:00","id":766361,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone, we had things go down in the game...and it all ended poorly. Essentially it came down to OOC problems manifesting within the game. The two players have a hard time gaming together and it's something our group has been working to fix for a while. Unfortunately the GM is often stuck in the middle trying to defend both sides to the others, and they get mad at the GM for not siding with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T22:03:40-08:00","id":766837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/763370-litany-question?p=766361#post766361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks everyone, we had things go down in the game...and it all ended poorly. Essentially it came down to OOC problems manifesting within the game. The two players have a hard time gaming together and it's something our group has been working to fix for a while. Unfortunately the GM is often stuck in the middle trying to defend both sides to the others, and they get mad at the GM for not siding with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yuck. This sort of sounds like the Silver Fang player might be drunk on power, trying to throw their weight around in-game to get back at the Ragabash. Hope your group can get this sorted- such petty things can tear groups apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}